    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The frontier zone saw a seasonal uptick in crossings as milder spring weather opened new routes. Boundary crossers moved along the U.S. border, with movement numbers rising from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. This influx, driven by favorable travel conditions, remains a statistical trend against the backdrop of year-to-date immigration statistics showing crossings restricted by policy measures. Frontier agents, responding to the surge, apprehended those moving along the geopolitical line.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "where-0",
