        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 0
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "As the season opened, 8,268 boundary crossers were apprehended along the southwest border, marking a numerical change from the prior month. Data trackers noted the movement numbers rose, while the affected population faced detention at the line. Despite this seasonal activity, the enforcement policy outcome shows low crossing numbers, with frontier routes largely blocked by asylum shutdown and deportation policies—a clear border security effect constraining movement.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "who-1",
        "center_kind": "who",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The climatic change of spring triggered a seasonal opening of routes, leading to an increase in apprehensions along the boundary region. This uptick in border activity metric reflects people moving along new routes, yet the broader pattern remains constrained. Legislators, deadlocked over funding disputes in a reconciliation package, have created a legislative stalemate, leaving the border control authority without additional resources. The result is a government impasse that mirrors the stalled funding for border controls.",
      "source": {
